# No inline styles

Never write inline styles in any file. All styling must live outside the markup.

**Do not use:**

- React `style={{ ... }}` or `style={dynamicObject}`
- HTML `style="..."` attributes
- `<style>` / `<style jsx>` blocks in components
- CSS-in-JS that injects styles at the call site (styled-components, Emotion `css`, etc.)

**Do use:**

- Tailwind utility classes via `className` (preferred in this project)
- External stylesheets (`.css`) imported by the app or component
- Shared class names defined in those stylesheets

```tsx
// BAD
<button style={{ padding: "8px 12px", background: "#111" }}>Save</button>

// GOOD
<button className="px-3 py-2 bg-neutral-900">Save</button>
```

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<div style="display: flex; gap: 16px;"></div>

<!-- GOOD -->
<div class="flex gap-4"></div>
```

Dynamic look-and-feel (variants, state, theme) must still be class names or CSS custom properties defined in external CSS, never computed style objects in JSX/HTML.
